<template><children>
        <li id="24.lp5"/>
    </children><heading>Dialog templates</heading><keywords><li>dialog</li><li>template</li><li>modal</li></keywords><section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p>Dialog definitions stay inert until an operation needs them. Keeping each dialog's markup, style, and initialization script in one child <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Element/template">HTML template</a> makes it a reusable UI unit with a fresh DOM lifetime on each mount. Shared modal styling belongs in the parent template so dialogs can use the same conventions and override them locally.</p>
    </section><section data-lp5-kind="code"><name>Dialog templates</name><code><![CDATA[
<template id="LP5-Dialog-Templates">
    <style> // dynamically inserted ahead of modal dialogs
        dialog:modal {
            max-width: 25rem;
            padding: 1.25rem;
        }

        dialog:modal button {
            padding: 0.6rem 1.2rem;
            font-size: 1rem;
        }

        dialog:modal [role="alert"] {
            color: #a00;
        }
    </style>
    ]]><lp5- ref="SelectCreateProject"/><![CDATA[
</template>
]]></code></section></template>
